    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IAtr">I Atr</ref> 4.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="220" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gif hwa hine forenne forstande, beon hy begen anes rihtes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="220" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.5"/> hwá<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.11"/> hine forne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.11"/> forstande, beon hi begen anes rihtes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="221" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis eum difforciet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.2"/>, sint ambo unius recti digni.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="4.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="54" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf hwá hine forne forstande, beon hi begen anes rihtes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="221" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IAtr_4-2.lnote.de.1"/> wenn jemand ihn [gewaltsam] vertheidigt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IAtr_4-2.lnote.de.2"/>, seien<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IAtr_4-2.lnote.de.3"/> sie beide gleicher Rechtsstrafe theilhaftig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone defends him [by force], let them both be subject to the same legal penalty.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IAtr_4-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="55" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone interposes in his defence<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IAtr_4-2.robnote.n.2"/>, they shall both incur the same punishment.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="221"><ref target="clause:IIAs_1-5">II As 1.5</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIAs_1-3">VI As 1.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II As. 1, 5; VI 1, 3</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_13-1">III Atr 13.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_33-1a">II Cn 33.1a</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II As 1.5; VI As 1.3.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">221</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">disfortiet <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">disfortiet T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">220</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">220</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">doppelt, aber einmal unterstrichen B</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">duplicated, but underlined once B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">148</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diese strengere Strafe für Begünstigung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8. 9ff.) hat VI As</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This stricter punishment for harbouring (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8. 9ff.) is found in VI As</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">148</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q versteht die Parallelen II Cn 53, 1 und II As 1, 5 richtig als <hi rend="italic">defendere presumat</hi> bzw. <hi rend="italic">obstabit</hi>. Vielleicht meint er hier ‘ihn [dem Strafvollzug] weigern, gewaltsam entreissen’. Die anderen Bedd. von <hi rend="italic">diffortiare</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi>) liegen ferner</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q correctly understands the parallels II Cn 53, 1 and II As 1, 5 as <hi rend="italic">defendere presumat</hi> and <hi rend="italic">obstabit</hi> respectively. Here perhaps he means ‘withhold him [from the execution of the penalty], wrest him away by force’. The other meanings of <hi rend="italic">diffortiare</hi> (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi>) are more remote</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">148</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dieselben 6 Worte III Atr 13 von dem neben dem Verletzer des Königsfriedens Betroffenen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The same 6 words in III Atr 13, of the person implicated together with the breaker of the king’s peace</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II As. 1, 5; VI, 1, 3; III Atr. 13; 13, 1.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IAtr_4-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. <hi rend="italic">forene forstande</hi>, VI As. 1, 4.</seg></note>
      </div>
